# Files bin/infra-update must find in a fetched tree before it will apply it.
#
# THIS LIST TRAVELS WITH THE TREE IT DESCRIBES, and that is the whole point.
# It used to be hardcoded in the updater, which meant the RUNNING version
# decided what the INCOMING version had to contain — so deleting a file from
# this repo made every existing cluster refuse every future commit, forever,
# retrying every five minutes and never saying anything except the name of a
# file that was removed on purpose. Renaming config/alertmanager.yml.tpl to
# bin/render-alertmanager did exactly that.
#
# A tree knows what it needs to deploy itself; the tree that came before it does
# not. Blank lines and # comments are ignored.

stacks/monitoring.yml
stacks/ingress.yml
stacks/admin.yml
config/vmagent.yml.tpl
config/alerts.yml
bin/render-alertmanager
bin/component
bin/stack-deploy
bin/infra-update
bin/render-fleet-env
bin/infra-images
bin/cloudflared-version
pki/__init__.py
signals/workloads.py
